Original commit body from 0f1521564b0b895cbc23d5cddd882f9f54441e1c:

The full-suite self-tree-validation job has been RED on dev on a matrix of
exactly {'cross_field|info': 9} -- nine ADR-0039 confidence-band violations,
all over-claims above the ast_call_direct ceiling of 0.85, four at exactly
1.0, the value confidence.py reserves on the principle that no detection
method is certain.

Three producers, and the obvious fix was wrong for one of them. The four 1.0
edges are toml_config's [project.scripts] defines_target edges, which never
passed an evidence_type and so inherited Edge.create's ast_call_direct
default -- "inferred from a direct (non-method) call site", which a
my-cli = "pkg.cli:main" line is not. The range check then judged a manifest
declaration against a call-site band. Lowering their confidence to fit would
have encoded the mislabel as truth: an entry that literally names its target
is not a low-confidence inference. Both toml sites now declare the registered
build_target_main pathway and drop the literal, deriving 0.95 at the ir.py
chokepoint with confidence_source=evidence_derived. The Cargo [[bin]]/[[test]]
site is unexercised by the self-corpus and was found by auditing the producer
rather than the violation list.

The other two declarations were already correct, so there the value moved to
the pathway instead: websocket.py's endpoint references edge hand-wrote 0.90
under a deliberate ADR-0028 fold, and java.py scaled a hardcoded 0.95 base by
the resolver multiplier (the multiplier is kept; only its base moves to the
registry seed).

Self-tree measured 9 -> 0; the matrix is now empty. The gate passes with NO
baseline change -- cross_field|info stays unbaselined at ceiling 0, since
baselining it at 9 would raise a ceiling the gate's own guidance says may
only ratchet down.

Scope, stated plainly: this fixes the three producers that fire, not the
class. A static producer audit found 32 out-of-band sites tree-wide; the
self-corpus exercises three. The remaining 29 (plus a computed-multiplier
cohort) are the unfinished ADR-0039 ruling-1 migration and are filed as
WI-famiv-gumof rather than left implicit -- most never declared a pathway at
all, so each needs a per-site judgment and some need new registrations.

Tests assert band membership via confidence_within_band against the registry
rather than golden numbers; the websocket one sweeps every emitted edge with
a non-vacuity guard. The pre-existing test_edge_confidence pinned
references == 0.90 -- the defect as expected behaviour -- and is corrected.

Refs: INV-zatug, WI-famiv-gumof
